== Usage ==
=== Combining Enchanted Books ===
An '''Anvil''' can be used to combine [[Enchanted Book]]s to increase their level, as in Vanilla Minecraft. it costs no additional {{Experience}} levels to do so, and as a result, gives no {{Skill|Enchanting}} experience. This does not work for all levels, however, as many high-level enchantments (usually level VI or higher) are obtained from [[Dungeons]], [[Experimentation Table|Experiments]], or the [[Dark Auction]].

=== Item Modifiers ===
An '''Anvil''' can be used to apply modifiers like [[Enchanted Book]]s, [[Endcap Enchantments]], {{Item|Hot Potato Book}} or {{Item|Book of Stats}} to an item.

=== Combining Tools ===
Two items of the same type can be combined to add their Enchantments. The item on the right slot will be deleted.

=== Applying Reforge Stones ===
{{Main|Reforge Stones}}
To apply a [[Reforge Stone]], place it on the right side of the '''Anvil''' and the item to reforge on the left side. Most Reforge Stones have a {{skill|mining}} skill requirement and a cost in {{C}} to apply.

=== Cosmetics ===
'''Anvil''' also can be used to apply [[Backpack Skins]], [[Power Orb Skins]], [[Helmet Skins]], [[Dyes|Custom Dyes]] and use {{Item|Ditto Blob}}.

== Trivia ==
* In SkyBlock, players cannot damage an Anvil by simply using it. The only known way of damaging an anvil in SkyBlock is by dropping it from a height larger than 1 block. The chance of the anvil getting damaged is 5% per block fallen. When an anvil gets damaged for the 1st time, it will turn into a {{Item|Chipped Anvil|link=}}. Damaging it again will turn it into a {{Item|Damaged Anvil|link=}}. Damaging it another time breaks it.

